From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:11:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-diting: Run the amplifier I2C
 bus at 400 kHz

Loading the CS35L41 speaker protection firmware writes 20 KB blocks; at
100 kHz they take about two seconds and the GENI I2C transfer times out
(1 s). 400 kHz is the vendor driver's default for this bus.

Local bring-up patch, not for upstream submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
index 276fdf1d2..850f9addd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
@@ -702,9 +702,13 @@ touchscreen@0 {
 	};
 };
 
-/* Loudspeaker amplifiers: Android I2C bus 2 = QUP SE15 */
+/*
+ * Loudspeaker amplifiers: Android I2C bus 2 = QUP SE15, at 400 kHz as the
+ * vendor driver's default: loading the protection firmware writes 20 KB
+ * blocks, which at 100 kHz exceed the GENI I2C 1 s transfer timeout.
+ */
 &i2c15 {
-	clock-frequency = <100000>;
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	/* vendor cs35l41@40 */
